## Files

```
top.v                  Top-level wrapper
modules/*.v            Per-layer Verilog
weights/weights.vh     Hardwired weight constants
kv_cache.v             KV cache (BRAM-mapped)
tb_top.py              Cocotb testbench
reference.py           Bit-exact Python reference
Makefile               Build targets: sim | synth-yosys | synth-vivado
synthesis/             Yosys, nextpnr, Vivado scripts
```

## Quick start

```bash
# Simulate (requires Verilator + cocotb)
make sim

# Synthesize for ECP5 with open-source tools
make synth-yosys

# Synthesize for Xilinx Artix-7 with Vivado
make synth-vivado
```

## Verification flow

The cocotb testbench drives random inputs through the RTL and compares
each output to the Python reference (`reference.py`). For deterministic
operations the comparison is bit-exact; for parallel reductions a small
tolerance is applied.

## Notes

- Multiplier strategy is selected per-precision; see [docs/rtl-generation](https://asicify.com/docs/rtl-generation).
- Weights are hardwired as constants — synthesis will fold them into the
  multiplier inputs (CSD / XNOR / Booth depending on quantization).
- For ASIC tape-out flows (sky130 + OpenLane), see
  [docs/targets/asic](https://asicify.com/docs/targets/asic).

